CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Forms a heterodimer with NS2B. Interacts with NS4B. Interacts
CC       with unphosphorylated RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5; this interaction
CC       stimulates RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5 guanylyltransferase
CC       activity. Interacts with non-structural protein 2A. Interacts with host
CC       SHFL; this interaction promotes NS3 degradation via a lysosome-
CC       dependent pathway. Interacts with host CEP63; this interaction
CC       disorganizes the centrosome and inhibits host innate immune response.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00066001}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Forms a heterodimer with serine protease NS3. May form
CC       homooligomers. Interacts with human SPCS1. Interacts with non-
CC       structural protein 2A. {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00064842}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Forms heterodimers with envelope protein E in the endoplasmic
CC       reticulum and Golgi. Interacts with non-structural protein 2A.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00065740}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer. Interacts with host SERTAD3; this interaction
CC       promotes capsid protein C degradation. Interacts with host CAPRIN1;
CC       this interaction is probably linked to the inhibition of stress
CC       granules formation by the virus. Interacts with host G3BP1; this
CC       interaction is probably linked to the inhibition of stress granules
CC       formation by the virus. {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00062625}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer; Homohexamer when secreted. Interacts with host
CC       TBK1. Interacts with host USP8. Interacts with envelope protein E.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00062141}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer; in the endoplasmic reticulum and Golgi. Interacts
CC       with host TYRO3, AXL and DC-SIGN proteins. Interacts with non-
CC       structural protein 2A. Interacts with host HAVCR1; this interaction
CC       likely mediates virus attachment to host cell. Interacts with host
CC       NCAM1. Interacts with host HSPA5. Interacts with Aedes aegypti SRPN25,
CC       APY and venom allergen-1 salivary proteins; the interactions do not
CC       affect Zika virus replication in human endothelial cells and
CC       keratinocytes. {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00064399}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with serine protease NS3. Interacts with NS1.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00065713}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with the structural protein prM/E complex, and the
CC       NS2B/NS3 protease complex. {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00063330}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: May interact with host ANKLE2; the interaction may cause
CC       defects in brain development, such as microcephaly. May interact with
CC       host SRPRA and SEC61G. {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00061840}.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Host cytoplasm, host perinuclear region
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00004407}. Host endoplasmic reticulum membrane
